  "commits": [
    {
      "sha": "4714a6208cb62323d36cae9883e18ef0afce0f0a",
      "html_url": "https://github.com/Anastasia-Labs/midgard/commit/4714a6208cb62323d36cae9883e18ef0afce0f0a",
      "message": "Merge remote-tracking branch 'origin/colll78/canonical-v1-watcher-l1-source-checkpoint' into p1/exec-onestep-push5",
      "authorName": "Philip DiSarro",
      "authorDate": "2026-10-21T09:57:50Z"
    },
    {
      "sha": "6e6620b177e26f31842409d6af8ffd8d02a43d59",
      "html_url": "https://github.com/Anastasia-Labs/midgard/commit/6e6620b177e26f31842409d6af8ffd8d02a43d59",
      "message": "Resolve a validation-trace canonical-decode step through its empty or item stages",
      "authorName": "Philip DiSarro",
      "authorDate": "2026-10-21T09:39:57Z"
    },
    {
      "sha": "072541a99bd9254f237c16a3ce8e22c80965c961",
      "html_url": "https://github.com/Anastasia-Labs/midgard/commit/072541a99bd9254f237c16a3ce8e22c80965c961",
      "message": "Alarm on a validation-trace thread waiting for an undriven one-step on our clock\n\nThe one-step-required wait now names the case, the thread, the step and\nour deadline, and raises the operator's alarm. Also tighten the wallet-move\ndeadline's case expiry to a number, restore a doc-comment paragraph break,\nand correct the installed-funding support's note on capacity pricing.",
      "authorName": "Philip DiSarro",
      "authorDate": "2026-10-21T09:16:54Z"
    },
    {
      "sha": "457a1ca0357883f1807e38940c8d576f8092eda1",
      "html_url": "https://github.com/Anastasia-Labs/midgard/commit/457a1ca0357883f1807e38940c8d576f8092eda1",
      "message": "Merge remote-tracking branch 'origin/colll78/canonical-v1-watcher-l1-source-checkpoint' into p1/exec-onestep-push4",
      "authorName": "Philip DiSarro",
      "authorDate": "2026-10-21T09:10:23Z"
    },
    {
      "sha": "d71308d379385acd88d5116f6c87fd601a6ec995",
      "html_url": "https://github.com/Anastasia-Labs/midgard/commit/d71308d379385acd88d5116f6c87fd601a6ec995",
      "message": "Test the validation-trace decode records under the prover funding permit in both directions\n\nA funded watcher with no publication observer refuses to run a dispute\nthat drives script selections, signing nothing; one whose roster does not\ngovern the script-decode contract stalls at the decode record that pays to\nit, and the case does not open; with both, it records the decode and then\nopens the case.",
      "authorName": "Philip DiSarro",
      "authorDate": "2026-10-21T08:58:52Z"
    },
    {
      "sha": "9a71bd159a2fe54465575f289faf83e5641efd44",
      "html_url": "https://github.com/Anastasia-Labs/midgard/commit/9a71bd159a2fe54465575f289faf83e5641efd44",
      "message": "Drive the remaining spend, output, signer and item context steps\n\nEach finishing step of the spend, output and signer stages, and the item\nsteps that head a sequence and finalize a frame, gets its own drive through\nthe resolution to the award, with the stage's refusal pinned.",
      "authorName": "Philip DiSarro",
      "authorDate": "2026-10-21T08:49:11Z"
    },
    {
      "sha": "7aaf6432a3bee476bb04c1362231d903ddd554d9",
      "html_url": "https://github.com/Anastasia-Labs/midgard/commit/7aaf6432a3bee476bb04c1362231d903ddd554d9",
      "message": "Resolve a validation-trace CEK context step through the finalize stage\n\nThe runner drives a CEK context step that finalizes a Cardano spend: the\nfinalize authenticate binds the step's redeemers control, the finalize\nspend writes the context's successor, and the context settle awards the\nthread. A finalization of any other purpose is left undriven.",
      "authorName": "Philip DiSarro",
      "authorDate": "2026-10-21T08:45:46Z"
    },
    {
      "sha": "23bc5b1b647a2dce9e2ee1fd6d6a4a555ba9a48d",
      "html_url": "https://github.com/Anastasia-Labs/midgard/commit/23bc5b1b647a2dce9e2ee1fd6d6a4a555ba9a48d",
      "message": "Refuse a wallet-paid validation dispute move only when it does not build\n\nThe funding permit no longer checks the wallet-move reserve at each thread\nmove our wallet pays. A move the wallet can fund lands, however far below\nthe reserve the wallet is; a move it cannot fund does not build and raises\nthe operator's named alarm, retried at each observation until a top-up\nlands it. The reserve is still kept when the case opens.",
      "authorName": "Philip DiSarro",
      "authorDate": "2026-10-21T08:34:37Z"
    },
    {
      "sha": "7689e7f27b8a30840477034914f5fddf63add1e7",
      "html_url": "https://github.com/Anastasia-Labs/midgard/commit/7689e7f27b8a30840477034914f5fddf63add1e7",
      "message": "Merge remote-tracking branch 'origin/colll78/canonical-v1-watcher-l1-source-checkpoint' into p1/exec-onestep-push3",
      "authorName": "Philip DiSarro",
      "authorDate": "2026-10-21T08:20:29Z"
    },
    {
      "sha": "7a9eb2bd38961b4a6fcf578399981fc5470f37ab",
      "html_url": "https://github.com/Anastasia-Labs/midgard/commit/7a9eb2bd38961b4a6fcf578399981fc5470f37ab",
      "message": "Price the validation dispute wallet-move reserve at the parameters of each turn\n\nThe reserve is a bound derived from the protocol parameters, so a\nreservation admitted at earlier parameters no longer refuses a permit minted\nat today's, and each move our wallet pays is checked against the reserve at\nthe fees of the turn that makes it. The funded test runner now prices each\nturn's policy at the emulator's current fees, as the watcher's funding\nfactory does with its fresh query.",
      "authorName": "Philip DiSarro",
      "authorDate": "2026-10-21T08:19:31Z"
    },
    {
      "sha": "137e9b23bf9c9bc8d58116f3f4b4e804e905f544",
      "html_url": "https://github.com/Anastasia-Labs/midgard/commit/137e9b23bf9c9bc8d58116f3f4b4e804e905f544",
      "message": "Fund each wallet-paid validation dispute move through the permit\n\nThe funding permit now checks the wallet-move reserve at every thread move\nour wallet pays, not only when the case opens, and prices the reserve at the\nprotocol's largest transaction size. A move the wallet cannot fund raises a\nnamed operator alarm naming the case, the thread and the move's deadline,\nreleases its reservation and retries at each observation until a top-up\nlands it.",
      "authorName": "Philip DiSarro",
      "authorDate": "2026-10-21T08:00:59Z"
    },
    {
      "sha": "6bcf2d3527de8afba8b628ede67bc1068ee3158c",
      "html_url": "https://github.com/Anastasia-Labs/midgard/commit/6bcf2d3527de8afba8b628ede67bc1068ee3158c",
      "message": "Drive a validation-trace CEK context item step that opens an item's tail in a data scan",
      "authorName": "Philip DiSarro",
      "authorDate": "2026-10-21T07:28:52Z"
    },
    {
      "sha": "4d796bdcb61a0d5f39e153b4ca7ceaf5c67ec9c5",
      "html_url": "https://github.com/Anastasia-Labs/midgard/commit/4d796bdcb61a0d5f39e153b4ca7ceaf5c67ec9c5",
      "message": "Document the builder balance error the validation-trace move fee matches",
      "authorName": "Philip DiSarro",
      "authorDate": "2026-10-21T07:26:01Z"
    },
    {
      "sha": "ac8f0b8a6c7fd4e490e51e7e78445deaf5a6ea2a",
      "html_url": "https://github.com/Anastasia-Labs/midgard/commit/ac8f0b8a6c7fd4e490e51e7e78445deaf5a6ea2a",
      "message": "Hold a validation-trace item chain move unless its thread history names one pending step\n\nThe shared item chain reads the pending item step from the thread's L1\nhistory. Any count of entry payments other than one now holds the run\nunder a named alarm instead of picking the last. A funded row drives a\nthread through the item chain, restarts the watcher mid-chain, and checks\nthe hold and the recovery once the history is whole.",
      "authorName": "Philip DiSarro",
      "authorDate": "2026-10-21T07:25:55Z"
    },
    {
      "sha": "76e9c4dbfa7077b73b0644fb555061c2b880c690",
      "html_url": "https://github.com/Anastasia-Labs/midgard/commit/76e9c4dbfa7077b73b0644fb555061c2b880c690",
      "message": "Resolve a validation-trace CEK context step through the redeemer select chain",
      "authorName": "Philip DiSarro",
      "authorDate": "2026-10-21T07:12:59Z"
    }
  ],
